### Order Tracking API - VS Code "REST Client" / JetBrains HTTP Client
### Seeded order numbers (user-001):
###   900001 PENDING | 900002 PENDING (already past expiry) | 900003 QUEUED
###   900004 IN_PROGRESS stale lease (HANG uid) | 900005 COMPLETED | 900006 FAILED (INVALID uid)
###   900007 DELAYED | 900008 EXPIRED | 900009 REFUNDED | 900010 QUEUED 30 min (stuck)

@base = http://localhost:8080
@user = user-001

### Health
GET {{base}}/healthz

##############################################################################
### 1) CORE ENDPOINTS
##############################################################################

### Create order (201). Re-send with the same key -> 200 + Idempotent-Replayed: true
# @name createOrder
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-001

{"user_id":"{{user}}","game_uid":"555666777","amount":120}

### Same key + different payload -> 422 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-001

{"user_id":"{{user}}","game_uid":"000000000","amount":999}

### Missing Idempotency-Key -> 400 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REQUIRED
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"user_id":"{{user}}","game_uid":"1","amount":10}

### Validation error -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (details per field)
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-bad-001

{"user_id":"","game_uid":"","amount":-5}

### Get order
GET {{base}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.order_no}}

### Get order - bad format -> 400 INVALID_ORDER_NO
GET {{base}}/orders/ORDER-123

### Get order - not found -> 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND
GET {{base}}/orders/ORD-20990101-123456

### List current tab
GET {{base}}/orders?tab=current&page=1&limit=10&user_id={{user}}

### List history tab
GET {{base}}/orders?tab=history&page=1&limit=10&user_id={{user}}

### List - invalid tab -> 400
GET {{base}}/orders?tab=foo

### Timeline
GET {{base}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.order_no}}/timeline

##############################################################################
### SCENARIO 3 - Bank webhook: signature / duplicate / late / out-of-order
### (POST /dev/webhooks/sign is a DEV-ONLY helper returning {body, signature})
##############################################################################

### 3.1 Sign a payment.succeeded event for the order created above
# @name signPay
POST {{base}}/dev/webhooks/sign
Content-Type: application/json

{"event_id":"evt-demo-001","order_no":"{{createOrder.response.body.$.order_no}}","type":"payment.succeeded","amount":120}

### 3.2 Deliver webhook -> result QUEUED
POST {{base}}/webhooks/payment
Content-Type: application/json
X-Signature: {{signPay.response.body.$.signature}}

{{signPay.response.body.$.body}}

### 3.3 Deliver the SAME event again (bank retry) -> DUPLICATE_IGNORED
POST {{base}}/webhooks/payment
Content-Type: application/json
X-Signature: {{signPay.response.body.$.signature}}

{{signPay.response.body.$.body}}

### 3.4 Wrong signature -> 401 INVALID_SIGNATURE
POST {{base}}/webhooks/payment
Content-Type: application/json
X-Signature: 0000deadbeef

{"event_id":"evt-forged","order_no":"ORD-20260101-900001","type":"payment.succeeded","amount":100}

### 3.5 Out-of-order: payment.failed arriving after success -> NOTED, status unchanged
# @name signFail
POST {{base}}/dev/webhooks/sign
Content-Type: application/json

{"event_id":"evt-demo-002","order_no":"{{createOrder.response.body.$.order_no}}","type":"payment.failed","amount":120}

###
POST {{base}}/webhooks/payment
Content-Type: application/json
X-Signature: {{signFail.response.body.$.signature}}

{{signFail.response.body.$.body}}

### 3.6 LATE webhook on EXPIRED order (seed 900008) -> AUTO_REFUNDED (not COMPLETED)
# @name signLate
POST {{base}}/dev/webhooks/sign
Content-Type: application/json

{"event_id":"evt-late-900008","order_no":"ORD-20260101-900008","type":"payment.succeeded","amount":450}

###
POST {{base}}/webhooks/payment
Content-Type: application/json
X-Signature: {{signLate.response.body.$.signature}}

{{signLate.response.body.$.body}}

###
GET {{base}}/orders/ORD-20260101-900008/timeline

### 3.7 Amount mismatch -> AMOUNT_MISMATCH (alert, status unchanged)
# @name signAmt
POST {{base}}/dev/webhooks/sign
Content-Type: application/json

{"event_id":"evt-amt-900001","order_no":"ORD-20260101-900001","type":"payment.succeeded","amount":1}

###
POST {{base}}/webhooks/payment
Content-Type: application/json
X-Signature: {{signAmt.response.body.$.signature}}

{{signAmt.response.body.$.body}}

##############################################################################
### SCENARIO 2 - Bots racing (run claim twice quickly with two bot IDs;
### each receives a DIFFERENT order or 204 - never the same one)
### Tip: set BOT_WORKERS=0 in docker-compose to drive bots manually.
##############################################################################

### Bot A claims
# @name claimA
POST {{base}}/bot/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{"bot_id":"manual-bot-A"}

### Bot B claims (gets another order / 204)
POST {{base}}/bot/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{"bot_id":"manual-bot-B"}

### Heartbeat (extends lease)
POST {{base}}/bot/orders/{{claimA.response.body.$.order_no}}/heartbeat
Content-Type: application/json

{"bot_id":"manual-bot-A"}

### Bot B tries to complete A's order -> 409 LEASE_LOST
POST {{base}}/bot/orders/{{claimA.response.body.$.order_no}}/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{"bot_id":"manual-bot-B","provider_ref":"ROGUE-1"}

### Bot A completes -> COMPLETED
POST {{base}}/bot/orders/{{claimA.response.body.$.order_no}}/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{"bot_id":"manual-bot-A","provider_ref":"TOPUP-REF-1"}

### Bot A completes AGAIN -> 409 (no second payment row)
POST {{base}}/bot/orders/{{claimA.response.body.$.order_no}}/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{"bot_id":"manual-bot-A","provider_ref":"TOPUP-REF-2"}

##############################################################################
### SCENARIO 4 - Top-up failure: transient vs permanent
##############################################################################

### 4.1 Transient (provider down) -> back to QUEUED with backoff, retry_count+1
# @name claimT
POST {{base}}/bot/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{"bot_id":"manual-bot-A"}

###
POST {{base}}/bot/orders/{{claimT.response.body.$.order_no}}/fail
Content-Type: application/json

{"bot_id":"manual-bot-A","error_code":"PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE","message":"503 from provider"}

### 4.2 Permanent (invalid UID) -> FAILED immediately
# @name claimP
POST {{base}}/bot/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{"bot_id":"manual-bot-A"}

###
POST {{base}}/bot/orders/{{claimP.response.body.$.order_no}}/fail
Content-Type: application/json

{"bot_id":"manual-bot-A","error_code":"INVALID_UID","message":"uid not found"}

### 4.3 Customer fixes the UID on FAILED seed order 900006 -> QUEUED (bots will complete it)
PATCH {{base}}/orders/ORD-20260101-900006/resolve
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-ID: {{user}}

{"action":"RETRY","game_uid":"600600600"}

### 4.4 Customer requests refund on DELAYED seed order 900007 -> REFUNDED
PATCH {{base}}/orders/ORD-20260101-900007/resolve
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-ID: {{user}}

{"action":"REFUND"}

### 4.5 Resolve a COMPLETED order -> 409 ORDER_NOT_RESOLVABLE
PATCH {{base}}/orders/ORD-20260101-900005/resolve
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-ID: {{user}}

{"action":"REFUND"}

### 4.6 Resolve someone else's order -> 403 FORBIDDEN
PATCH {{base}}/orders/ORD-20260101-900006/resolve
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-ID: hacker

{"action":"REFUND"}

### 4.7 End-to-end with built-in bots: UID prefix drives the mock provider
###     INVALID* -> FAILED, DOWN* -> retries then DELAYED, FLAKY* -> random, HANG* -> bot crash
# @name createInvalid
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-invalid-001

{"user_id":"{{user}}","game_uid":"INVALID-42","amount":50}

##############################################################################
### SCENARIO 1 - Bot crashed / stale lease
### Seed 900004 is IN_PROGRESS by "bot-dead" with a 10-minute-old lease.
##############################################################################

### Trigger the scheduler tick now (normally every SCHEDULER_INTERVAL)
POST {{base}}/admin/maintenance/run

### 900004 is back to QUEUED with retry_count=1 (HANG uid -> crashes again -> eventually DELAYED)
GET {{base}}/orders/ORD-20260101-900004/timeline

### The dead bot wakes up and heartbeats -> 409 LEASE_LOST
POST {{base}}/bot/orders/ORD-20260101-900004/heartbeat
Content-Type: application/json

{"bot_id":"bot-dead"}

##############################################################################
### SCENARIO 5 - QR expiry / stuck orders / customer report
##############################################################################

### Seed 900002 is PENDING past expiry -> run maintenance -> EXPIRED.
### Seed 900010 queued 30 min -> "ALERT order queued beyond SLA" in logs.
POST {{base}}/admin/maintenance/run

###
GET {{base}}/orders/ORD-20260101-900002

### Customer reports issue on the stuck order 900010 -> escalated to DELAYED (if still QUEUED)
POST {{base}}/orders/ORD-20260101-900010/report-issue
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-ID: {{user}}

{"reason":"ยังไม่ได้รับไอเทม","description":"จ่ายไปนานแล้ว"}

### Report on a completed order -> recorded on timeline, no status change
POST {{base}}/orders/ORD-20260101-900005/report-issue
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-ID: {{user}}

{"reason":"ไอเทมไม่เข้า"}

###
GET {{base}}/orders/ORD-20260101-900010/timeline
